@startuml
title Transactional File Download and Replacement
start

:Validate required JSON identity / parent fields;
:Compute canonical local path;
:Require valid Microsoft fileSystemInfo.lastModifiedDateTime;
if (Authoritative timestamp unavailable or invalid?) then (yes)
  :Record download failure;\ndo not manufacture a timestamp;
  stop
endif

if (Microsoft reports malware?) then (yes)
  :Reject download and notify user;
  stop
endif

:Read expected file size and available online hash metadata;
:Capture pre-existing canonical / DB baseline when applicable;
:Check local free space and reservation;
if (Insufficient local disk space?) then (yes)
  :Record download failure;
  stop
endif

if (~--dry-run?) then (yes)
  :Simulate successful download / state transition;
else (no)
  :Download through onedrive.d / curlEngine.d\nto private <canonical>.partial staging file;
  note right
    The existing canonical file is left untouched while data
    is transferred. A failed HTTP response or incomplete transfer
    is never promoted into the user's real pathname.
  end note

  if (Final HTTP response is not successful?) then (yes)
    :Retry when applicable or report failure;
    :Retain existing canonical file;
    stop
  endif

  :Build neutral commit information\n(size and streamed/generated hashes);

  if (Download validation enabled?) then (yes)
    :Compare downloaded hash and reported online hash;
    :Compare size for validation / diagnostics;
    if (Hash validation fails?) then (yes)
      :Reject and remove private staging file;
      :Retain canonical file and applied DB baseline;
      stop
    endif
  else (no)
    :Skip content-integrity rejection by configuration;
  endif

  :Re-evaluate canonical file at commit boundary;
  note right
    The canonical file is checked again at the last responsible
    moment because it may have changed locally while the online
    replacement was being downloaded.
  end note
  if (Canonical contains unique local content\nnot matching incoming online or DB baseline?) then (yes)
    :Create and verify non-destructive safeBackup copy;
    note right
      LOCAL DATA LOSS PREVENTION

      The staged online replacement must not overwrite unique local
      bytes. A verified safeBackup copy is required before commit,
      and the canonical pathname remains present while this happens.
    end note
    if (safeBackup preservation fails?) then (yes)
      :Reject staged replacement;
      :Retain canonical file and DB state;
      note right
        Preservation is mandatory. If safeBackup cannot be verified,
        the client refuses to replace the user's canonical local file.
      end note
      stop
    endif
  else (no)
    note right
      No safeBackup is needed when the local file still matches the
      last applied DB baseline, or already matches the incoming online
      content. In those cases there is no unique local content to save.
    end note
  endif

  :Recheck canonical existence / content after inspection;
  if (Canonical changed while commit was prepared?) then (yes)
    :Discard staged replacement;\nlocal activity wins this race;
    stop
  endif

  :Atomically promote .partial to canonical path;
  if (Promotion fails?) then (yes)
    :Record failure and retain any existing canonical file;
    stop
  endif

  :Apply authoritative Microsoft timestamp;
endif

:Save applied online item in DB;
note right
  The DB is advanced only after the corresponding local state
  has actually been committed. It must not claim that online
  content is applied when the canonical replacement failed.
end note
if (write_xattr_data enabled?) then (yes)
  :Write OneDrive metadata xattr;
endif
:Record transfer success / metrics;
stop
@enduml
